Hi there,

I am still struggling with this. I have now compared glPca() and gl.pcoa() with an additional data and am getting similar inconsistencies in the scores between the two functions. I now know that I do want to scale my data, so these are the two scripts that I am using to create the PCA.

male.pca1 <- glPca(male.gl <http://male.gl/>, center = TRUE, scale = TRUE, nf = NULL, loadings = TRUE,
                     alleleAsUnit = FALSE, useC = TRUE, parallel = FALSE,

                     n.cores = NULL, returnDotProd=FALSE, matDotProd=NULL)     ### with 4 axis

male.pca3 <- gl.pcoa(male.gl <http://male.gl/>, nfactors= 4)

Does anyone have any experience with this? Can anyone please advise how I know which one is giving the correct answer?
Many thanks,
Lana

